[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2427020538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2427020538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2427020538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QqWT6","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T15:30:32Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T15:30:32Z","body":"I'm not sure about the comma syntax, it's basically a weird `and` that allows multiple definitions. I think single definition is enough in most cases.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2427020538/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428056375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2428056375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2428056375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QuTM3","user":{"login":"zjin123","id":184326668,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvyaDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184326668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123","html_url":"https://github.com/zjin123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-22T02:00:45Z","updated_at":"2024-10-22T05:35:00Z","body":"> I'm not sure about the comma syntax, it's basically a weird `and` that allows multiple definitions. I think single definition is enough in most cases.\r\n\r\nBoth the comma syntax and multiple definitions / conditions are borrowed from Swift ([optional binding](https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/documentation/the-swift-programming-language/thebasics/#Optional-Binding)). As a Swift user, the comma syntax appears more readable than `and` keyword to me personally,  but of course it can be changed to other syntax which may be more suitable for GDScript.\r\n\r\nAs for multiple definitions / conditions, it is mainly for static typing. While GDScript is a dynamic typing language, some people like me actually use it with static typing as much as possible. Static typing will introduce extra code. For example, consider dragging:\r\n\r\nWithout static typing:\r\n```\r\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\r\n\tif event is InputEventMouseButton && event.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT:\r\n\t\tif event.is_pressed():\r\n\t\t\tstart_dragging(event)\r\n\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\tstop_dragging(event)\r\n\telif dragging && event is InputEventMouseMotion:\r\n\t\tdo_dragging(event)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs very readable. But if one write it with static typing (maybe for performance and static checking):\r\n```\r\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\r\n\tif event is InputEventMouseButton:\r\n\t\tvar mouseButtonEvent := event as InputEventMouseButton\r\n\t\tif mouseButtonEvent.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT:\r\n\t\t\tif mouseButtonEvent.is_pressed():\r\n\t\t\t\tstart_dragging(mouseButtonEvent)\r\n\t\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\t\tstop_dragging(mouseButtonEvent)\r\n\telif dragging && event is InputEventMouseMotion:\r\n\t\tvar mouseMotionEvent := event as InputEventMouseMotion\r\n\t\tdo_dragging(mouseMotionEvent)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf only one definition / condition is allowed, the first `if` (in the dynamic typing one) has to be split into two `if` as one can only call `button_index` on the casted result with static typing.\r\n\r\nWith static typing and multiple conditions:\r\n```\r\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\r\n\tif var mouseButtonEvent := event as InputEventMouseButton, mouseButtonEvent.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT:\r\n\t\tif mouseButtonEvent.is_pressed():\r\n\t\t\tstart_dragging(mouseButtonEvent)\r\n\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\tstop_dragging(mouseButtonEvent)\r\n\telif dragging, var mouseMotionEvent := event as InputEventMouseMotion:\r\n\t\tdo_dragging(mouseMotionEvent)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis one requires less code lines and is as readable as the first dynamic typing one. Multiple conditions is useful for code with static typing. Code with dynamic typing perhaps do not need it at all.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428056375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428996725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2428996725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2428996725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Qx4x1","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-22T11:13:45Z","updated_at":"2024-10-22T11:13:45Z","body":"Still, the comma syntax should be a separate proposal and separate PR IMO. Can you split it?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428996725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2434068008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2434068008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2434068008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RFO4o","user":{"login":"zjin123","id":184326668,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvyaDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184326668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123","html_url":"https://github.com/zjin123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-24T01:57:40Z","updated_at":"2024-10-24T01:57:40Z","body":"Sure. I close this PR for now and will reopen it when split is done.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2434068008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2437982051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2437982051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2437982051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RUKdj","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T14:31:54Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T14:31:54Z","body":"@zjin123 You created two separate commits, but @KoBeWi suggested to create two separate PRs.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2437982051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439080931","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2439080931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2439080931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RYWvj","user":{"login":"zjin123","id":184326668,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvyaDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184326668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123","html_url":"https://github.com/zjin123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T00:28:33Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T00:28:33Z","body":"> @zjin123 You created two separate commits, but @KoBeWi suggested to create two separate PRs.\r\n\r\nThanks for the reminder. I just opened another PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98538 for the first commit.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439080931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439217091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-2439217091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":2439217091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RY3_D","user":{"login":"zjin123","id":184326668,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvyaDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184326668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123","html_url":"https://github.com/zjin123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zjin123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T03:19:56Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T03:19:56Z","body":"The reason of using comma here is that `and` or `&&` is not suitable with variable definition. Because when either `and` or `&&` is used directly after variable definition, they will become part of the variable initializer. For example,\r\n```\r\nif var x = 1 and y == 2:\r\n\tprint(x) # x is true\r\n\r\nif var x = 1 and foo(x): # analyzer error: x is not defined\r\n\tprint(x)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo fix it:\r\n```\r\nif (var x = 1) and y == 2:\r\n\tprint(x) # x is int\r\n\r\nif (var x = 1) and foo(x):\r\n\tprint(x) # x is int\r\n```\r\nThe one works but requires additional parentheses.\r\n\r\nWith comma syntax, it is simple:\r\n```\r\nif var x = 1, y == 2:\r\n\tprint(x) # x is int\r\n\r\nif var x = 1, foo(x):\r\n\tprint(x) # x is int\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439217091/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3720656953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-3720656953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":3720656953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dxLg5","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T20:29:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T20:29:32Z","body":"I suggest you look into the already implemented [match statement guard patterns](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#pattern-guards)\r\n\r\nI think what makes the most sense here is something like:\r\n```gdscript\r\nif var x = 1 when x != 5:\r\n    # x is not 5\r\n\r\nif var x = randf() when x > 0.5:\r\n    # This has a 50% chance of happening, and I have the random float stored in x.\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3720656953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3720894575","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98335#issuecomment-3720894575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98335","id":3720894575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dyFhv","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T21:31:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T21:46:02Z","body":"I thought about this issue a bit more, and shouldn't just evaluating declarations and definitions be enough?\r\n```gdscript\r\nif var x = 1, foo(x):\r\n    print(x) # x is int\r\n```\r\nShould become:\r\n```gdscript\r\nif foo(var x = 1):\r\n    print(x) # x is int\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn this case\r\n```gdscript\r\nif var x = 1 and y == 2:\r\n    print(x) # x is true\r\n```\r\nx isn't really used in the conditional which means if we want to only check if y equals 2 this can be rewritten as:\r\n```gdscript\r\nif y == 2:\r\n    int x = 1\r\n    print(x) # x is int \r\n```\r\n\r\nThe idea here is that the `=` operator should always return the right hand operand, as suggested in #7222\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar x = 3 + 5 # returns 8\r\nvar y = x # returns x (8)\r\nx = y * 2 # returns y * 2 (16)\r\n\r\nprint(var z = x + y) # prints x + y (24)\r\n```\r\nThe discussion in #7222 concluded that this is very problematic, but I think maybe have it give you a warning or even an error by default when writing statements like `if x = y:`? Or maybe only allow `if var x = y:`?\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\nseems like KoBeWi was 2 steps ahead of me on that warning idea :P [comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/20634#issuecomment-409255010)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3720894575/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]